component mc_group "PLCopen MC Part 4 axes group of a 4R palletizer: MC_MoveDirectAbsolute over mc_axis members through palletkins";
author "SyncTwin";
license "GPL";

description
"""
An axes group (PLCopen Motion Control Part 4) of the 4R palletizer whose
kinematics is *palletkins* (src/emc/kinematics/palletkins.c): members 0..3 =
base turn, shoulder, elbow, flange turn (deg); the group's coordinates are
X Y Z (flange point, mm, base frame) and C (flange turn, deg).  The kinematics
is compiled into the component from palletkins.c itself (no second copy of the
formulas); the geometry is pins of the instance, the same seven numbers as the
pins of the palletkins kinematics module, so one machine twin feeds both.
One instance per group (the group number = the instance number).
Built like any component of this tree: palletkins.c is included by its path
under src/ (src/ is on the include path of the tree's RT build).  Built alone
with halcompile, palletkins.c sits next to this file (halcompile puts the
component's directory on the include path).

MEMBERS: four *mc_axis*(9) instances.  The group owns their motion inputs:
joint-cmd-N -> mc_axis.N.position, joint-vel-N -> .velocity,
joint-acc-N -> .acceleration, member-execute / member-halt / member-reset
-> .execute / .halt / .reset of every member (one period pulses).  It reads
.actual-position (joint-fb-N), .state, .command-id, .done-id, .aborted-id,
.failed-id and the limits the axis is given (joint-maxv/maxa/min/max-N, the
same signals as the axis's maxv/maxa/min-limit/max-limit).  MC_Power stays
per axis: the group never powers a member.

COMMANDS (rising edges, numbered on command-id like mc_axis; resolved on
done-id / aborted-id / failed-id): *execute* = a move to position-x..c
(MC_POSITION X Y Z A B C) in *coord* (0 ACS: the elements 0..3 are the member
positions, 4..5 must be 0; 1 MCS: through the inverse kinematics, A and B must
be 0 - the flange is kept level; of the four configurations of palletkins
(inverse flags: shoulder front/back, elbow up/down) a Direct move takes the one
nearest to the move's start among those within the members' soft limits, a
Linear move stays in the configuration it starts in; none reachable is 10,
reachable only outside the limits is 5; 2 PCS: refused, no part frame yet) with *mode*
0 MC_MoveDirectAbsolute or 1 MC_MoveLinearAbsolute (MCS only) and
*buffer-mode* 0 mcAborting / 1 mcBuffered (one move queued; 2..5 blending
is not implemented: such a move runs buffered - it stops exactly at the
corner, the programmed path itself; a Linear move
aborts nothing and is not aborted by a move: refused 2 while the group moves,
halt it or buffer it); *halt* =
MC_GroupHalt (every member halts; Done when all stand); *reset* = MC_GroupReset
(the members in ErrorStop get MC_Reset; Done when none is left).  *enable* is
the level of MC_GroupEnable/MC_GroupDisable.

DIRECT MOVE: joint interpolated, synchronized - every member runs the same
normalized trapezoid s(t) in [0,1] with peak ds/dt = V = min maxv_i/|d_i| and
d2s/dt2 = A = min maxa_i/|d_i| (d_i the member's distance), so member i gets
velocity V*|d_i| and acceleration A*|d_i|, never over its own limits, and all
start and stop together (from standstill; an aborting move from motion
follows each member's own blend).  A Direct move ignores velocity, acceleration,
deceleration and jerk (Part 4: it runs at the mechanism's limits).

LINEAR MOVE: the flange point on a straight line (C interpolated with it;
a pure turn of C runs on C, velocity then in deg/s) with a trapezoid of
*velocity*, *acceleration* (0 = the mechanism's: the least maxa_i/|dq_i/ds|
along the path), *deceleration* (0 = acceleration; jerk must be 0).  The members are put into SynchronizedMotion (member-sync ->
mc_axis.N.sync-enable) and given the inverse kinematics of the path every
period (joint-sync-N -> mc_axis.N.sync-pos).  Where the path asks a member
for more than its maxv the path slows down for that period (velocity
override by the joint limits).  At the end the position is held one period
(the members stop at zero velocity), then sync is released; Done when every
member stands.  MC_GroupHalt decelerates the path at *deceleration*.  A
point of the path without an inverse solution, or a member leaving
SynchronizedMotion, is an ErrorStop (10, 13): sync is released and the
members decelerate at their maxa.

STATE CODES (pin *state*, Part 4 group diagram): 0 GroupDisabled,
1 GroupStandby, 2 GroupMoving (a halt too), 5 GroupErrorStop
(3 GroupHoming, 4 GroupStopping: not produced).  The state is derived from
the members' states and the group's own command: no second machine.

ERROR IDS (pin *error-id*: newest outcome; *group-error-id*: why the group is
in ErrorStop): 2 command not allowed
in this state, 5 member target outside its soft limits, 7 invalid geometry or
member limits, 8 unknown or not implemented mode, 10 target unreachable (no
inverse solution), 11 A/B not 0 (MCS) or elements 4..5 not 0 (ACS),
12 coordinate system not supported (PCS), 13 a member failed (its error-id
says why; the others are halted).

ONE MULTIPLEXED FB, as mc_axis: the outputs belong to the newest command;
Done, CommandAborted and a refusal Error stay while its input is held and are
reset one period after it falls.  *actual-x* .. *actual-c* are the forward
kinematics of joint-fb every period (MC_GroupReadActualPosition).
""";

pin in real shoulder_x "palletkins.shoulder-x";
pin in real shoulder_z "palletkins.shoulder-z";
pin in real upper "palletkins.upper";
pin in real fore "palletkins.fore";
pin in real flange_x "palletkins.flange-x";
pin in real flange_y "palletkins.flange-y";
pin in real flange_z "palletkins.flange-z";

pin in bool enable "MC_GroupEnable (1) / MC_GroupDisable (0)";
pin in bool execute "rising edge: the move described by mode/coord/buffer-mode/position-*";
pin in bool halt "rising edge: MC_GroupHalt";
pin in bool reset "rising edge: MC_GroupReset";
pin in sint mode "0 MoveDirectAbsolute, 1 MoveLinearAbsolute";
pin in sint coord "MC_COORD_SYSTEM: 0 ACS, 1 MCS, 2 PCS";
pin in sint buffer_mode "MC_BUFFER_MODE: 0 mcAborting, 1 mcBuffered, 2..5 blending (run buffered)";
pin in real velocity "Linear move: path velocity, mm/s";
pin in real acceleration "Linear move: path acceleration, mm/s^2";
pin in real deceleration "Linear move: path deceleration, mm/s^2";
pin in real jerk "Linear move: path jerk, mm/s^3";
pin in real position_x "MC_POSITION.X, mm (ACS: member 0)";
pin in real position_y "MC_POSITION.Y, mm (ACS: member 1)";
pin in real position_z "MC_POSITION.Z, mm (ACS: member 2)";
pin in real position_a "MC_POSITION.A, deg (ACS: member 3)";
pin in real position_b "MC_POSITION.B, deg: must be 0";
pin in real position_c "MC_POSITION.C, deg (ACS: must be 0)";

pin in real joint_fb_#[4] "mc_axis.N.actual-position";
pin in real joint_maxv_#[4] "= mc_axis.N.maxv";
pin in real joint_maxa_#[4] "= mc_axis.N.maxa";
pin in real joint_min_#[4] "= mc_axis.N.min-limit";
pin in real joint_max_#[4] "= mc_axis.N.max-limit";
pin in sint joint_state_#[4] "mc_axis.N.state";
pin in uint joint_command_id_#[4] "mc_axis.N.command-id";
pin in uint joint_done_id_#[4] "mc_axis.N.done-id";
pin in uint joint_aborted_id_#[4] "mc_axis.N.aborted-id";
pin in uint joint_failed_id_#[4] "mc_axis.N.failed-id";

pin out real joint_cmd_#[4] "to mc_axis.N.position";
pin out real joint_vel_#[4] "to mc_axis.N.velocity";
pin out real joint_acc_#[4] "to mc_axis.N.acceleration";
pin out real joint_sync_#[4] "to mc_axis.N.sync-pos (Linear move)";
pin out bool member_sync "to mc_axis.N.sync-enable of every member (Linear move)";
pin out bool member_execute "to mc_axis.N.execute of every member";
pin out bool member_halt "to mc_axis.N.halt of every member";
pin out bool member_reset "to mc_axis.N.reset of every member";

pin out sint state "group state code";
pin out bool busy;
pin out bool done;
pin out bool active;
pin out bool command_aborted;
pin out bool error;
pin out sint error_id "outcome of the newest command: refusal code, else the ErrorStop reason";
pin out sint group_error_id "MC_GroupReadError: why the group is in ErrorStop, 0 outside it";
pin out uint command_id;
pin out uint active_id "number of the command the group executes now (a buffered one waits), 0 none";
pin out uint done_id;
pin out uint aborted_id;
pin out uint failed_id;
pin out real actual_x;
pin out real actual_y;
pin out real actual_z;
pin out real actual_c;

variable int seq;          // last command number given out
variable int owner;        // input of the newest command: 1 execute 2 halt 3 reset, 0 none
variable int term_shown;   // a terminal output has been out one period
variable int cmd_err;      // refusal of the newest command
variable int grp_err;      // ErrorStop reason
variable int run;          // what the members run for the group: 0 none, 1 move, 2 halt, 3 reset
variable int run_id;       // its command number
variable int ex_old;
variable int halt_old;
variable int reset_old;
variable int fire;         // member pulse to raise next: 1 execute 2 halt 3 reset
variable double tj[4];     // member targets of the running (last issued) move
variable int inv[4];       // member takes part in the running command
variable int learned[4];   // its command number is known
variable unsigned cid0[4]; // member command-id when the pulse went out
variable unsigned ours[4]; // member command number of the running command
variable int q_valid;      // a buffered move waits
variable int q_mode;       // its mode: 0 direct, 1 linear
variable double q_p[4];    // linear: target X Y Z C
variable double q_v;
variable double q_a;
variable double q_d;
variable int lin;          // linear phase: 1 members entering sync, 2 path, 3 hold one period, 4 members stopping
variable int lin_wait;     // periods spent in phase 1
variable int lin_halt;     // MC_GroupHalt: decelerate the path to a stop
variable double lp0[4];    // path start X Y Z C
variable double lp1[4];    // path end
variable double l_len;     // path length (mm, or deg of C for a pure turn)
variable double l_s;       // path position
variable double l_v;       // path velocity
variable double l_vmax;
variable double l_acc;
variable double l_dec;
variable double qc[4];     // member positions given this period
variable int q_id;
variable double q_tj[4];
variable int l_flags;      // linear: the palletkins configuration (inverse flags) the path keeps

function _;
;;

/* palletkins.c compiled in: its module entry points, license line and exported
 * symbols (EXPORT_SYMBOL, KINS_NOT_SWITCHABLE) stay inside this component
 * (hidden; renamed so as not to clash with halcompile's own).  Its `static struct geom *g` is pointed at this instance's
 * geometry pins before every call (one thread: no other caller in between). */
#include <rtapi_math.h>   /* before the hidden scope: libm's declarations keep default visibility */
#pragma push_macro("rtapi_app_main")
#pragma push_macro("rtapi_app_exit")
#pragma push_macro("MODULE_LICENSE")
#pragma push_macro("EXPORT_SYMBOL")
#undef rtapi_app_main
#undef rtapi_app_exit
#undef MODULE_LICENSE
#undef EXPORT_SYMBOL
#define rtapi_app_main palletkins_app_main_unused
#define rtapi_app_exit palletkins_app_exit_unused
#define MODULE_LICENSE(s)
#define EXPORT_SYMBOL(x)   /* a hidden export would leave the .ver line empty (Makefile awk takes column 6) */
#pragma GCC visibility push(hidden)
#if __has_include("emc/kinematics/palletkins.c")
#include "emc/kinematics/palletkins.c"   /* in the tree: src/ is on the include path */
#else
#include "palletkins.c"                   /* halcompile: next to this file */
#endif
#pragma GCC visibility pop
#pragma pop_macro("EXPORT_SYMBOL")
#pragma pop_macro("MODULE_LICENSE")
#pragma pop_macro("rtapi_app_exit")
#pragma pop_macro("rtapi_app_main")

#define E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE 2
#define E_SOFT_LIMIT 5
#define E_INVALID_PARAMETERS 7
#define E_UNKNOWN_MODE 8
#define E_UNREACHABLE 10
#define E_ORIENTATION 11
#define E_COORD_SYSTEM 12
#define E_MEMBER_FAILED 13

#define GS_DISABLED 0
#define GS_STANDBY 1
#define GS_MOVING 2
#define GS_ERROR_STOP 5
#define AX_ERROR_STOP 7     /* mc_axis ST_ERROR_STOP */

#define RUN_NONE 0
#define RUN_MOVE 1
#define RUN_HALT 2
#define RUN_RESET 3
#define RUN_LIN 4
#define AX_STANDSTILL 1     /* mc_axis ST_STANDSTILL */
#define AX_SYNC 5           /* mc_axis ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION */

static void use_geometry(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, struct geom *gi) {
    gi->sx = __comp_inst->shoulder_x_p; gi->sz = __comp_inst->shoulder_z_p; gi->u = __comp_inst->upper_p;
    gi->f = __comp_inst->fore_p; gi->fx = __comp_inst->flange_x_p; gi->fy = __comp_inst->flange_y_p;
    gi->fz = __comp_inst->flange_z_p;
    g = gi;
}

/* The move's member targets into out[4] from the start seed[4]; 0 or a refusal code.  MCS: every palletkins
 * configuration (inverse flags) is solved, the nearest to seed within the members' soft limits wins (Direct); a
 * Linear move keeps the configuration of seed (its path cannot change it). */
static int resolve(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, const double *seed, double *out) {
    struct geom gi;
    double jt[EMCMOT_MAX_JOINTS] = {0}, d, best_d = 1e300;
    EmcPose p = {{0, 0, 0}, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
    KINEMATICS_FORWARD_FLAGS ff = 0;
    KINEMATICS_INVERSE_FLAGS fi = 0, fl, fl_start = 0;
    int i, ok, e;
    if (buffer_mode < 0 || buffer_mode > 5) return E_UNKNOWN_MODE;
    if (mode != 0 && mode != 1) return E_UNKNOWN_MODE;
    if (mode == 1) {
        if (coord != 1) return E_COORD_SYSTEM;
        if (!(velocity > 0.0 && acceleration >= 0.0 && deceleration >= 0.0 && jerk == 0.0)) return E_INVALID_PARAMETERS;
    }
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++)
        if (!(joint_maxv(i) > 0.0 && joint_maxa(i) > 0.0 && joint_max(i) > joint_min(i))) return E_INVALID_PARAMETERS;
    if (coord == 0) {
        if (position_b != 0.0 || position_c != 0.0) return E_ORIENTATION;
        out[0] = position_x; out[1] = position_y; out[2] = position_z; out[3] = position_a;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (out[i] < joint_min(i) || out[i] > joint_max(i)) return E_SOFT_LIMIT;
        return 0;
    }
    if (coord == 2) return E_COORD_SYSTEM;
    if (coord != 1) return E_UNKNOWN_MODE;
    if (!(upper > 0.0 && fore > 0.0)) return E_INVALID_PARAMETERS;
    if (position_a != 0.0 || position_b != 0.0) return E_ORIENTATION;
    p.tran.x = position_x; p.tran.y = position_y; p.tran.z = position_z; p.c = position_c;
    use_geometry(__comp_inst, &gi);
    if (mode == 1) {   /* the configuration of the start: the forward kinematics reports it */
        EmcPose ps;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) jt[i] = seed[i];
        kinematicsForward(jt, &ps, &ff, &fl_start);
    }
    e = E_UNREACHABLE;
    for (fl = 0; fl < 4; fl++) {
        if (mode == 1 && fl != fl_start) continue;
        fi = fl;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) jt[i] = seed[i];
        if (kinematicsInverse(&p, jt, &fi, &ff) != 0) continue;
        e = E_SOFT_LIMIT;
        for (ok = 1, d = 0.0, i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            if (jt[i] < joint_min(i) || jt[i] > joint_max(i)) ok = 0;
            d += fabs(jt[i] - seed[i]);
        }
        if (ok && d < best_d) { best_d = d; for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) out[i] = jt[i]; }
    }
    return best_d < 1e300 ? 0 : e;
}

/* Synchronized Direct move to t[4] from the actual member positions: one normalized trapezoid for all. */
static void issue_move(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, const double *t, int id) {
    double V = 1e300, A = 1e300, dd;
    int i;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        dd = fabs(t[i] - joint_fb(i));
        if (dd > 0.0) {
            if (joint_maxv(i) / dd < V) V = joint_maxv(i) / dd;
            if (joint_maxa(i) / dd < A) A = joint_maxa(i) / dd;
        }
    }
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        dd = fabs(t[i] - joint_fb(i));
        tj[i] = t[i];
        joint_cmd_set(i, t[i]);
        /* a member that stays: a null move at its limits (mc_axis refuses velocity 0) */
        joint_vel_set(i, dd > 0.0 ? V * dd : joint_maxv(i));
        joint_acc_set(i, dd > 0.0 ? A * dd : joint_maxa(i));
    }
    run = RUN_MOVE; run_id = id; fire = 1;
    if (id == (int)command_id) active_set(1);
}

static void issue_members(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int what, int id, int only_errorstop) {
    int i;
    run = what; run_id = id; fire = what == RUN_HALT ? 2 : 3;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) inv[i] = !only_errorstop || joint_state(i) == AX_ERROR_STOP;
}

/* Members at path fraction f (0..1) of the running Linear move, in its configuration l_flags; 0 or -1 (no solution). */
static int path_ik(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, double f, double *out) {
    struct geom gi;
    double jt[EMCMOT_MAX_JOINTS] = {0};
    EmcPose p = {{0, 0, 0}, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
    KINEMATICS_FORWARD_FLAGS ff = 0;
    KINEMATICS_INVERSE_FLAGS fi = l_flags;
    int i;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) jt[i] = qc[i];
    p.tran.x = lp0[0] + (lp1[0] - lp0[0]) * f; p.tran.y = lp0[1] + (lp1[1] - lp0[1]) * f;
    p.tran.z = lp0[2] + (lp1[2] - lp0[2]) * f; p.c = lp0[3] + (lp1[3] - lp0[3]) * f;
    use_geometry(__comp_inst, &gi);
    if (kinematicsInverse(&p, jt, &fi, &ff) != 0) return -1;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) out[i] = jt[i];
    return 0;
}

/* The mechanism's path acceleration (acceleration 0 = the mechanism's ceiling, as mc_axis's 0 = maxa): the least
 * maxa_i / |dq_i/ds| over PATH_SAMPLES pieces of the path; -1 if a piece has no inverse solution. */
static void to_errorstop(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int id);
#define PATH_SAMPLES 64   /* ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ, не замер: 64 pieces resolve |dq/ds| of a 4R arm along one line */
static double mech_acc(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    double best = 1e300, keep[4], qa[4], qb[4], h = 1.0 / PATH_SAMPLES, dqds;
    int n, i;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) keep[i] = qa[i] = qc[i];
    for (n = 0; n < PATH_SAMPLES && l_len > 0.0; n++) {
        if (path_ik(__comp_inst, (n + 1) * h, qb)) { best = -1.0; break; }
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            dqds = fabs(qb[i] - qa[i]) / (h * l_len);
            if (dqds > 0.0 && joint_maxa(i) / dqds < best) best = joint_maxa(i) / dqds;
            qa[i] = qc[i] = qb[i];
        }
    }
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) qc[i] = keep[i];
    return best;
}

/* Linear move from the members' actual positions to p1 (X Y Z C), member targets t (resolved): the members enter
 * SynchronizedMotion first; t is the running move's end (tj), the start of a move buffered after it. */
static void start_linear(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, const double *p1, const double *t, double v, double a, double d, int id) {
    struct geom gi;
    double jf[EMCMOT_MAX_JOINTS] = {0}, dx, dy, dz;
    EmcPose p = {{0, 0, 0}, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
    KINEMATICS_FORWARD_FLAGS ff = 0;
    KINEMATICS_INVERSE_FLAGS fi = 0;
    int i;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) { qc[i] = jf[i] = joint_fb(i); joint_sync_set(i, qc[i]); lp1[i] = p1[i]; tj[i] = t[i]; }
    use_geometry(__comp_inst, &gi);
    kinematicsForward(jf, &p, &ff, &fi);
    l_flags = fi;
    lp0[0] = p.tran.x; lp0[1] = p.tran.y; lp0[2] = p.tran.z; lp0[3] = p.c;
    dx = lp1[0] - lp0[0]; dy = lp1[1] - lp0[1]; dz = lp1[2] - lp0[2];
    l_len = sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz);
    if (l_len == 0.0) l_len = fabs(lp1[3] - lp0[3]);
    l_s = 0.0; l_v = 0.0; l_vmax = v;
    run = RUN_LIN; run_id = id;
    if (a <= 0.0 || d <= 0.0) {
        double m = mech_acc(__comp_inst);
        if (m < 0.0) { to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_UNREACHABLE); return; }
        if (a <= 0.0) a = m;
    }
    l_acc = a; l_dec = d > 0.0 ? d : a;
    lin = 1; lin_wait = 0; lin_halt = 0;
    member_sync_set(1);
    if (id == (int)command_id) active_set(1);
}

/* The running command ends: done (0), aborted (1) or failed (2); its outputs only while it is the newest. */
static void end_run(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int how) {
    int mine = busy && run_id == (int)command_id;
    if (run_id) {
        if (how == 0) done_id_set(run_id); else if (how == 1) aborted_id_set(run_id); else failed_id_set(run_id);
    }
    if (mine) {
        if (how == 0) done_set(1); else if (how == 1) command_aborted_set(1);
        term_shown = 0; busy_set(0); active_set(0);
    }
    run = RUN_NONE; run_id = 0; fire = 0;
}

static void to_errorstop(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int id) {
    if (run) end_run(__comp_inst, 2);
    member_sync_set(0); lin = 0;   /* the members decelerate at their maxa */
    if (q_valid) { failed_id_set(q_id); q_valid = 0; }
    grp_err = id; cmd_err = 0;
    busy_set(0); active_set(0);
    state_set(GS_ERROR_STOP);
}

static void next_from_queue(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    if (!q_valid) return;
    q_valid = 0;
    if (q_id == (int)command_id) busy_set(1);
    if (q_mode == 1) start_linear(__comp_inst, q_p, q_tj, q_v, q_a, q_d, q_id);
    else issue_move(__comp_inst, q_tj, q_id);
}

/* One period of the Linear move (run == RUN_LIN). */
static void linear_step(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, double dt) {
    double rem, vreq, vn, ds, qn[4], r, st;
    int i, k, all = 1, err;
    if (lin == 1) {   /* the members enter SynchronizedMotion */
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (joint_state(i) != AX_SYNC) all = 0;
        if (all) lin = 2;
        else if (++lin_wait > 2) { to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_MEMBER_FAILED); return; }
        if (lin == 1) return;
    }
    if (lin >= 2) for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (lin < 4 && joint_state(i) != AX_SYNC) { to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_MEMBER_FAILED); return; }
    if (lin == 2) {
        rem = l_len - l_s;
        vreq = lin_halt ? 0.0 : l_vmax;
        if (sqrt(2.0 * l_dec * rem) < vreq) vreq = sqrt(2.0 * l_dec * rem);
        vn = vreq > l_v ? (vreq < l_v + l_acc * dt ? vreq : l_v + l_acc * dt)
                        : (vreq > l_v - l_dec * dt ? vreq : l_v - l_dec * dt);
        ds = 0.5 * (l_v + vn) * dt;
        if (ds >= rem || (!lin_halt && rem <= 0.0)) ds = rem;
        err = l_len > 0.0 ? path_ik(__comp_inst, (l_s + ds) / l_len, qn) : (qn[0] = qc[0], qn[1] = qc[1], qn[2] = qc[2], qn[3] = qc[3], 0);
        /* velocity override by the joint limits: the step shrinks until every member is within its maxv */
        for (k = 0; !err && k < 8; k++) {
            r = 0.0;
            for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) { st = fabs(qn[i] - qc[i]) / (joint_maxv(i) * dt); if (st > r) r = st; }
            if (r <= 1.0) break;
            ds /= r; vn = 2.0 * ds / dt - l_v; if (vn < 0.0) vn = 0.0;
            err = path_ik(__comp_inst, (l_s + ds) / l_len, qn);
        }
        if (err) { to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_UNREACHABLE); return; }
        l_s += ds; l_v = vn;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) { qc[i] = qn[i]; joint_sync_set(i, qn[i]); }
        if (l_s >= l_len || (lin_halt && l_v == 0.0)) { lin = 3; lin_wait = 0; }
    } else if (lin == 3) {   /* the last position held one period (the members' velocity goes to 0), then released */
        if (++lin_wait >= 2) { member_sync_set(0); lin = 4; }
    } else if (lin == 4) {
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (joint_state(i) != AX_STANDSTILL) all = 0;
        if (all) { lin = 0; end_run(__comp_inst, 0); next_from_queue(__comp_inst); }
    }
}

FUNCTION(_) {
    int ex_edge = execute && !ex_old, halt_edge = halt && !halt_old, reset_edge = reset && !reset_old;
    int i, all, any_failed, any_aborted, any_axis_err = 0, e;
    double t[4], seed[4];
    struct geom gi;
    double jf[EMCMOT_MAX_JOINTS] = {0};
    EmcPose p = {{0, 0, 0}, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
    KINEMATICS_FORWARD_FLAGS ff = 0;
    KINEMATICS_INVERSE_FLAGS fi = 0;
    ex_old = execute; halt_old = halt; reset_old = reset;

    /* member pulses are one period long; a pulse waits one low period after the previous one */
    if (member_execute || member_halt || member_reset) {
        member_execute_set(0); member_halt_set(0); member_reset_set(0);
    } else if (fire) {
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            cid0[i] = joint_command_id(i); learned[i] = 0;
            if (fire == 1) inv[i] = 1;
        }
        if (fire == 1) member_execute_set(1); else if (fire == 2) member_halt_set(1); else member_reset_set(1);
        fire = 0;
    }

    /* terminal outputs (PLCopen Part 1, 2.4.1), as mc_axis */
    {
        int held = (owner == 1 && execute) || (owner == 2 && halt) || (owner == 3 && reset);
        if (done || command_aborted || cmd_err) {
            if (term_shown && !held) { done_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); cmd_err = 0; }
            term_shown = 1;
        }
    }
    if (ex_edge || halt_edge || reset_edge) {
        cmd_err = 0; command_aborted_set(0); done_set(0); term_shown = 0; busy_set(0); active_set(0);
        owner = ex_edge ? 1 : halt_edge ? 2 : 3;
        seq = seq == 0x7fffffff ? 1 : seq + 1;
        command_id_set(seq);
    }

    /* the members' answers to the running command, by their numbers */
    if (run == RUN_LIN) linear_step(__comp_inst, period * 1e-9);
    else if (run && !fire && !member_execute && !member_halt && !member_reset) {
        all = 1; any_failed = 0; any_aborted = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            if (!inv[i]) continue;
            if (!learned[i] && joint_command_id(i) != cid0[i]) { ours[i] = joint_command_id(i); learned[i] = 1; }
            if (!learned[i]) { all = 0; continue; }
            if (joint_failed_id(i) == ours[i]) any_failed = 1;
            else if (joint_aborted_id(i) == ours[i]) any_aborted = 1;
            else if (run == RUN_RESET ? joint_state(i) == AX_ERROR_STOP : joint_done_id(i) != ours[i]) all = 0;
        }
        if (any_failed && run == RUN_MOVE) { member_halt_set(1); to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_MEMBER_FAILED); }
        else if (any_failed || any_aborted) end_run(__comp_inst, 1);
        else if (all) {
            if (run == RUN_RESET) grp_err = 0;
            end_run(__comp_inst, 0);
            next_from_queue(__comp_inst);
        }
    }

    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (joint_state(i) == AX_ERROR_STOP) any_axis_err = 1;

    /* derived state */
    if (!enable) {
        if (run) { int was_move = run == RUN_MOVE; end_run(__comp_inst, 1); if (was_move) fire = 2; }   /* members halt */
        member_sync_set(0); lin = 0;   /* a Linear move: the members decelerate at their maxa */
        if (q_valid) { aborted_id_set(q_id); q_valid = 0; }
        state_set(GS_DISABLED);
    } else if (state == GS_DISABLED) {
        state_set(GS_STANDBY);
    }
    if (enable && any_axis_err && state != GS_ERROR_STOP && run != RUN_RESET) to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_MEMBER_FAILED);
    if (state != GS_ERROR_STOP && state != GS_DISABLED) state_set(run == RUN_MOVE || run == RUN_HALT || run == RUN_LIN || q_valid ? GS_MOVING : GS_STANDBY);

    /* this period's command */
    if (ex_edge) {
        if (state == GS_DISABLED || state == GS_ERROR_STOP || run == RUN_HALT) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        else if (state == GS_MOVING && buffer_mode >= 1) {   /* buffered; blending runs buffered (exact stop) */
            if (q_valid) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
            else if ((e = resolve(__comp_inst, tj, t))) cmd_err = e;
            else {
                for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) q_tj[i] = t[i];
                q_p[0] = position_x; q_p[1] = position_y; q_p[2] = position_z; q_p[3] = position_c;
                q_mode = mode; q_v = velocity; q_a = acceleration; q_d = deceleration;
                q_id = seq; q_valid = 1; busy_set(1);
            }
        } else if (state == GS_MOVING && (mode == 1 || run == RUN_LIN)) {
            cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;   /* a Linear move neither aborts nor is aborted by a move */
        } else {
            for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) seed[i] = joint_fb(i);
            if ((e = resolve(__comp_inst, seed, t))) cmd_err = e;
            else {
                if (run) end_run(__comp_inst, 1);
                if (q_valid) { aborted_id_set(q_id); q_valid = 0; }
                busy_set(1); state_set(GS_MOVING);
                if (mode == 1) { double p1[4] = {position_x, position_y, position_z, position_c};
                                 start_linear(__comp_inst, p1, t, velocity, acceleration, deceleration, seq); }
                else issue_move(__comp_inst, t, seq);
            }
        }
    } else if (halt_edge) {
        if (state == GS_DISABLED || state == GS_ERROR_STOP) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        else if (state == GS_STANDBY) { done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(seq); }
        else if (run == RUN_LIN) {   /* the path decelerates itself; the move is aborted, the halt owns the run */
            if (run_id) aborted_id_set(run_id);
            if (q_valid) { aborted_id_set(q_id); q_valid = 0; }
            run_id = seq; lin_halt = 1; busy_set(1); active_set(1);
        } else {
            if (run) end_run(__comp_inst, 1);
            if (q_valid) { aborted_id_set(q_id); q_valid = 0; }
            issue_members(__comp_inst, RUN_HALT, seq, 0); busy_set(1); active_set(1); state_set(GS_MOVING);
        }
    } else if (reset_edge) {
        if (state != GS_ERROR_STOP) {
            if (state == GS_DISABLED || state == GS_STANDBY) { done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(seq); }
            else cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        } else if (!any_axis_err) {
            grp_err = 0; state_set(GS_STANDBY); done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(seq);
        } else {
            issue_members(__comp_inst, RUN_RESET, seq, 1); busy_set(1); active_set(1);
        }
    }
    if (cmd_err && (ex_edge || halt_edge || reset_edge)) failed_id_set(seq);

    group_error_id_set(state == GS_ERROR_STOP ? grp_err : 0);
    active_id_set(run ? run_id : 0);
    error_set(cmd_err != 0 || (state == GS_ERROR_STOP && !busy && !done));
    error_id_set(cmd_err ? cmd_err : state == GS_ERROR_STOP ? grp_err : 0);

    use_geometry(__comp_inst, &gi);
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) jf[i] = joint_fb(i);
    kinematicsForward(jf, &p, &ff, &fi);
    actual_x_set(p.tran.x);
    actual_y_set(p.tran.y);
    actual_z_set(p.tran.z);
    actual_c_set(p.c);
}
